2. OUT OF SCOPE BY DECISION

   These are not defects the mitigation skipped. They are changes of a different
   shape and size, each of which needs its own reviewed plan.

   2.1 Credential storage: unsalted MD5 -> password_hash() / PASSWORD_BCRYPT
       (CWE-916). Every stored credential is an unsalted MD5 digest, and the
       digest is produced or compared at nine sites in seven files - five writes
       (User.class.php:354 and :446, public/Installation.class.php:105,
       api/UserInterface.class.php:413 and :548) and four comparison-side sites
       (Authentication_Password.class.php:34 and
       Authentication_Basic.class.php:35, which build the digest they compare
       with, public/Login.class.php:116 as md5($password) == $row, and
       vcalendar.php:89). That split is what the migration has to work against:
       the writes are what a rehash must change, the comparisons are what a
       dual-format window must accept. COUNT CORRECTED in fix round 1 - the
       first consolidation said "six places" over a list of nine sites and did
       not say which were writes. The mitigation only removed the comparison
       from SQL in vcalendar.php (it now fetches by username and compares in PHP
       with hash_equals()) and left the format alone; the format is why the
       pass-the-hash item exists at all, and
       Authentication_Password.class.php:34 still accepts a client-supplied
       `_hash` in place of a password. Changing the storage format is a
       migration - rehash on next successful login, a dual-format acceptance
       window, the GWT login, and a decision about accounts that never log in
       again - not a patch.

   2.2 Library-wide prepared statements. The mitigation parameterized by the
       established idiom on the reachable and in-scope surface (->quote() for
       values, intval()/casts for numeric ids, a validated-identifier helper for
       schema and column names; the plan counted 252 pre-existing ->quote( sites
       setting the precedent, and the sweep added more). Moving the whole
       library to prepared statements is a rewrite
       with its own regression surface, and the identifier half of the problem
       cannot be bound at all - it still needs a validator.

   2.3 The vendored phpGACL/adodb copies under
       lib/org/freemedsoftware/acl/ (notably acl/adodb/). Their string
       concatenation is library-internal and upstream-maintained: note it, do
       not fork it. 67 of the concatenation gate's 76 remaining allowlist
